{
  "$comment": "EXP-1291 Threads v2: THE session card ×4 — a session inside a thread (the root's own session first, every child where its `session` card message sits, an agent channel's `thread_started` cards) is ONE card = the Work card's HEADER row (work-card.json geometry.header px, radius lg, card hairline, no shadow): the state `icon` (concept), the `name` (medium, truncates), the muted `kindWord`, trailing the muted `elapsed` (tabular figures) with a 12px spinner in front while `running`. No device, account, branch or other caption. Tapping it opens that session's raw view (today's session view). Model = pure `sessionCard(session, title, now)` (TS reference packages/domain-contract/src/session-tree.ts; mirrors desktop domain::session_tree, iOS ExpCore SessionTree.swift, Android domain/SessionTree.kt), every mirror replays `cases` and compares the WHOLE expected object. state = `ended` when status ended, else `needs_you` when needsInput, else `blocked` when blocked is set, else `queued` when status queued, else `working` when busy, else `waiting`. name = `title`, the session's display title (EXP-1341 session-title.json `sessionTitle`; never `Session N`). elapsed = startedAt → now (ended: → endedAt, else updatedAt), the work card's ladder ('37s', '2m 04s', '1h 03m'); null while queued or without a parsable startedAt. running = state working. tone = `tones[state]`. EXP-1323: `caption` = the session's trimmed live status line (synced `sessions.caption`, device-written on tool edges, throttled, <=80 chars, cleared at turn end) as the card's muted second line; blank/absent = null; an ended session's caption drops unless `aside` (a /btw answer keeps its first line). NEW-1: `blocked.kind` names why (contract codingSessionBlocked.kinds); `copy.blockedKinds[kind]` is the state word for it (an unknown kind reads `copy.states.blocked`); the server holds needsInput while blocked, so the card reads Needs you first.",
